I can distinguish **four principal lines of writing**, but I cannot reliably identify the individual letterforms in this rendering well enough to produce a defensible diplomatic transcription. Supplying Aramaic words here would risk substituting conjecture or remembered text for visible ink.

Please provide the original-resolution photograph or separate, unresampled crops of each line. I would distinguish:
- `[...]` — physical loss at a fragment edge or lacuna;
- `א֯` — an identifiable but doubtful letter;
- visible, unidentifiable ink traces — explicitly described as such, **not** marked as missing leather.

I cannot responsibly supply a line-by-line square-script text from this image without guessing.
